/-- **Encode after decode.** Every public part and codeword is the honest encoding of its own decoding, for every
primitive and coins. For a rate-1 scheme with no `pp` this says `Dec` is a bijection with inverse `Enc`, so a
server-supplied codeword that decodes to `W` is exactly `Enc(W)`. -/
def Scheme.EncDec (sch : Scheme M) : Prop :=
  ∀ (pp : Bits sch.t) (C : sch.Code) (ω : M.Ω) (r : sch.Coins),
    sch.enc (sch.dec pp C (M.answer ω)) ω r = (pp, C)


